{"status":"completed","summary":"Created appworker on node1 and configured persistent login-session limits of 8,192 open files and 256 processes. Verified both soft and hard limits before and after reboot. The installed RHEL release and kernel were unchanged.","actions_performed":["Created appworker with /home/appworker and /bin/bash.","Added /etc/security/limits.d/99-appworker-limits.conf with root ownership and mode 0644.","Set soft and hard nofile limits to 8192.","Set soft and hard nproc limits to 256.","Safely rebooted node1 and verified recovery and persistence."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Create the appworker account","command_ids":["cmd-2e735d28fd7542b4","cmd-286c9d16a5e04f1f"],"summary":"The account exists with UID/GID 1000, /home/appworker, and /bin/bash; its home persisted across reboot."},{"requirement":"Limit appworker login sessions to 8,192 open files and 256 processes","command_ids":["cmd-14e3af67c68b4b74","cmd-3b800b4ec43d4209","cmd-286c9d16a5e04f1f"],"summary":"Persistent PAM limits set both soft and hard nofile to 8192 and nproc to 256. A login-style runuser session directly confirmed all four effective values before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-5e0de8269fa84897","cmd-286c9d16a5e04f1f"],"summary":"RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64 remained installed after the change and reboot."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-34e0d7b77194490d","cmd-2706f3b6e8974bbf","cmd-354bec10c4924cda","cmd-286c9d16a5e04f1f"],"summary":"Healthy baseline used boot ID 6aa805ba-5845-488d-af03-a621555936e2; systemd acknowledged the scheduled reboot; node1 returned running with changed boot ID f7121625-b136-4574-b703-b3431f58b1d8; the account, home, limits file, and effective limits all recovered."}]}
